<hick:session xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0" start="2026-08-22T13:01:02Z">
<hick:user>Priya's export is data/checkout-latency.csv in this folder: one row per four-hour bucket (columns bucket_start, p95_ms, requests) from 2026-08-10 to 2026-08-23. The meeting upstream of this document decided what to measure. Please: (1) paste, by reference, the meeting turn where Priya warns about the load-test window, so the reader sees why rows are excluded; (2) add a python3 hick:exec cell (container image python:3.12, mount this directory and read the CSV relatively) that prints the mean bucket p95 for a pre-deploy baseline (2026-08-10 to 2026-08-12), the broken window (2026-08-12 00:00 to the fix at 2026-08-21 12:00), and after the fix (2026-08-21 12:00 to 2026-08-24), excluding the bucket covering the 2026-08-18 10:00-12:00 load test, and says how many rows it excluded; pin the output with hick:expect match=exact; (3) under a '## Findings' heading write the results as short hick:copy fragments with class=finding (ids p95-before-after, load-test-excluded, baseline) that a downstream document can quote; (4) run verify until the cell passes. Keep prose short.</hick:user>
